# env.example — the NAMES of the secret settings this project needs, never their values.
# Copy this file to .env on your own computer and fill in the values there.
# .env is ignored by git: never commit it and never paste a secret into a chat.
# (No leading dot on purpose: the project's deny rule on .env.* keeps guarding real secret files.)
#
# Right now nothing needs a secret: the engine uses your own Cursor and GitHub (gh) logins.
# When a phase adds a service that needs a key, add its name here in the same change,
# with an empty value and a one-line comment saying what it is for, for example:
#
# # Payment provider, test mode (Phase 6)
# PAYMENTS_API_KEY=
